  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Request path",
      "collapsed": false,
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": [],
      "description": "Follow the service path or find the trace for one invoice."
    },
    {
      "type": "nodeGraph",
      "title": "Service graph",
      "description": "Which service calls which, over the selected time range. Each edge is a client span paired with its server span by Tempo's metrics generator: the gRPC quote (API → billing), the Relay's HTTP calls back into the API, PostgreSQL, and the RabbitMQ hops when the RabbitMQ.Client publish and consume spans pair. \"user\" is a caller that sends no spans (k6, curl). Click a node or an edge for its rate, error ratio and latency. Not filtered by the Service variable.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "tempo",
            "uid": "tempo"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "serviceMap"
        }
      ],
      "options": {},
      "id": 2,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Follow one renewal",
      "description": "Where did this renewal go? Paste the invoice id returned by POST /subscriptions/{id}/renewals into \"Invoice id\" at the top. The API tags its spans with invoice.id and Wolverine tags every saga message with wolverine.saga.id (the saga id is the invoice id), so this lists the traces that touched that renewal. Open the trace id for the waterfall: API → billing quote (gRPC) → outbox row → relay → RabbitMQ → saga → payments → relay → API. Empty until an id is entered.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "tempo",
            "uid": "tempo"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "limit": 20,
          "tableType": "traces",
          "query": "{ span.wolverine.saga.id = \"$invoice_id\" || span.invoice.id = \"$invoice_id\" }"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "id": 3,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Traces",
      "collapsed": false,
      "id": 4,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 12
      },
      "panels": [],
      "description": "Find renewal traces, requests reaching Payments, and failed spans."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Renewal traces",
      "description": "The latest orchestrated renewals: traces whose API span name contains \"renewals\" (POST /subscriptions/{id}/renewals). Open one to follow it through billing, payments and the relay.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "tempo",
            "uid": "tempo"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "limit": 20,
          "tableType": "traces",
          "query": "{ resource.service.name = \"subscription-management\" && name =~ \".*renewals.*\" }"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "id": 5,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Traces reaching Payments",
      "description": "Which traces include both the API and payments? Finds both services in the same trace, including renewal charges and cancellation refunds. Open the waterfall to inspect parent-child continuity; this search does not assert an ancestor relationship between the two services.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "tempo",
            "uid": "tempo"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "limit": 20,
          "tableType": "traces",
          "query": "{ resource.service.name = \"subscription-management\" } && { resource.service.name = \"payments\" }"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "id": 6,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 13
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Error traces",
      "description": "Traces with a failed span in the selected services: a 5xx response, a failed gRPC call, or a message handler that threw. Open one to see which hop failed.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "tempo",
            "uid": "tempo"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "limit": 20,
          "tableType": "traces",
          "query": "{ resource.service.name =~ \"$service\" && status = error }"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "id": 7,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 13
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Edges between services (Tempo service graph metrics)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "id": 8,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22
      },
      "panels": [],
      "description": "Compare traffic, errors, latency, and missing span pairs across service edges."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Edge rate",
      "description": "Calls per second on each client → server edge. The connection type is empty for HTTP and gRPC, messaging_system for a hop through RabbitMQ, database for PostgreSQL and virtual_node when the other end sends no spans. Not filtered by the Service variable.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (client, server, connection_type) (rate(traces_service_graph_request_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{client}} → {{server}} {{connection_type}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "id": 9,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Edge error ratio",
      "description": "Share of the calls on each edge whose client or server span ended in error (0% for an edge without failures). Tells which hop is failing, where a per-service error rate only says that something is.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(sum by (client, server) (rate(traces_service_graph_request_failed_total[$__rate_interval])) or sum by (client, server) (rate(traces_service_graph_request_total[$__rate_interval])) * 0) / sum by (client, server) (rate(traces_service_graph_request_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{client}} → {{server}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "gradientMode": "none"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "id": 10,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 23
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Edge p95",
      "description": "95th percentile of the time the called service spent on a request (its own server or consumer span), per edge. Compare with the caller's view in the trace to see time lost on the network or in a queue.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, client, server) (rate(traces_service_graph_request_server_seconds_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{client}} → {{server}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "gradientMode": "none"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "id": 11,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 9,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Broker transit p95",
      "description": "How long messages wait in RabbitMQ: 95th percentile of the gap between the end of the publish span and the start of the consume span, per producer → consumer edge. Only the RabbitMQ.Client spans can pair (the consume span is a child of the publish span); no data while messages flow means they do not — read the gap from the trace waterfall instead.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, client, server) (rate(traces_service_graph_request_messaging_system_seconds_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{client}} → {{server}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "gradientMode": "none"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "id": 12,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 9,
        "x": 9,
        "y": 31
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Unpaired spans",
      "description": "Client, server, producer and consumer spans per second that Tempo could not pair into an edge within its wait window (expired edges, from Tempo's own /metrics). A steady baseline under load is expected: Wolverine's send and receive spans are siblings and never pair. A jump means a hop stopped propagating trace context and its edge is missing from the graph.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(tempo_metrics_generator_processor_service_graphs_expired_edges[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 1
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      },
      "id": 13,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 31
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Operations per service (Tempo span metrics)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "id": 14,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 39
      },
      "panels": [],
      "description": "Compare request rates, errors, and duration by service operation."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Operation rate",
      "description": "Requests per second handled by each service, by server span name: HTTP endpoints (METHOD route) and gRPC methods. Shows which entry points a flow exercises in every service, including the ones without a k6 script.",
