    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Wolverine dead letters · failures",
      "description": "Dead letters: messages per second a service gave up on after its retry policy and moved to its dead-letter storage; must stay at zero, anything else needs a manual replay. Failures: handler executions that threw, including the attempts that were retried successfully. Counters are emitted on the first matching failure or dead letter; an empty panel has no failure samples, so check the inbox and operation panels for telemetry health.",
